The [original #4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says “one issue, one fix queued.”
Its own report view separates two causes. They need separate tickets because the parser and the booking form fail in different ways.

## What the desk can count

<SplitSummary />

These counts follow `uniqueById`, `causeOf` and `groupByCause` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`,
with each report’s tenant from `src/lib/data/tenants/`. One report ID counts once.
Intake’s browser-locale tag is a guess; it does not decide the cause.

## Parser: day-first dates read month first

The shared parser reads dates as month/day for tenants who write day/month.
The day and month swap. Reports from app and email, and from forms without the booking-v3 hint,
belong to the [parser ticket](https://github.com/saucy-tech/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
The five one-day reports above remain in the parser count because that is where the desk’s exported logic files them.
Their wording alone does not establish a third cause or a separate engineering outcome.

## Hint: booking-v3 tells people to type the wrong format

Booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, but its form reads dates in the tenant’s day-first format.
The affected form reports come from alder.physio, copper.studio and pale.harbour.
Changing the shared parser does not fix that mismatch. They belong to the
[hint ticket](https://github.com/saucy-tech/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Engineering update: closed 2026-10-05

<Callout>
The live Challenge page reports: parser <strong>FIXED</strong>, <code>fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales</code>;
hint <strong>WON’T FIX</strong>, booking-v3 form retired. Retiring a form is not evidence that its hint was corrected.
</Callout>

Source: [engineering update on the Challenge page](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows),
checked 2026-10-28. The supplied kb was exported 2026-10-04, so it predates that update.
Ticket outcomes must reflect this newer evidence.

## Triage after #4471

The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) says to merge by normalized subject.
Its component compares causes instead. Identical subjects can describe these two different problems;
different subjects can describe the same cause. Read the report, resolve its tenant and channel,
and merge only when the cause matches. Keep uncertain reports visible for review.

[Accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) records the old policy.
It remains unchanged as the record of that decision. A replacement policy needs a new decision record.

